Licence and reuse terms: unclear

The legal text in this repository was copied by script from the Gibraltar Laws website
(https://www.gibraltarlaws.gov.gi), published by the Government of Gibraltar. The PDFs carry the line
"(c) Government of Gibraltar (www.gibraltarlaws.gov.gi)". The site states no licence and gives no terms for
reuse. Its copyright-and-disclaimer page (https://www.gibraltarlaws.gov.gi/copyright-and-disclaimer) says only,
in its disclaimer:

  "Please note that it cannot be guaranteed that a document available on-line exactly reproduces an
  officially adopted text. Only Government of Gibraltar legislation published in paper editions of the
  Gibraltar Gazette and Supplements is deemed authentic."

Until the Government of Gibraltar confirms reuse terms, this repository is PRIVATE and must not be made public or
redistributed. If it is ever published, credit the source exactly as:

  (c) Government of Gibraltar (www.gibraltarlaws.gov.gi), as published at gibraltarlaws.gov.gi, with changes to
  layout only (white space and page furniture). The Gibraltar Gazette is the authentic text.

The scripts in tools/ were written by Lexifina and are the only part of this repository that Lexifina licenses.
